Adds an optional ordered `path` of point IDs to the existing SRJ connection for each explicitly declared multi-pad differential trace. These excerpts show the connection names and pair metadata. Each connection also carries its existing `pointsToConnect` geometry.

Matching explicit paths attached to named nets are preserved as their own SRJ connections. Test-point taps remain in the residual net connection.

## Before

```json
{
  "connections": [
    { "name": "source_trace_0" },
    { "name": "source_trace_1" }
  ],
  "differentialPairs": [
    {
      "connectionNames": ["source_trace_0", "source_trace_1"],
      "lengthTolerance": 0.1
    }
  ]
}
```

## After

```json
{
  "connections": [
    {
      "name": "source_trace_0",
      "path": ["pcb_port_0", "pcb_port_2", "pcb_port_4"]
    },
    {
      "name": "source_trace_1",
      "path": ["pcb_port_1", "pcb_port_3", "pcb_port_5"]
    }
  ],
  "differentialPairs": [
    {
      "connectionNames": ["source_trace_0", "source_trace_1"],
      "lengthTolerance": 0.1
    }
  ]
}
```

The companion PR defines and consumes the field in the autorouter. [tscircuit/tscircuit-autorouter#3643](https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit-autorouter/pull/3643)

## Summary

Makes the quote easier to read: one table with every expense, its total and its per-board price, ending with a grand total that includes shipping and taxes. The details stay available underneath.

![Quote page summary for the dual RP2350 board: 5 PCBs, 2 assembled](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tscircuit/circuit-json-to-jlcpcb-quote/2f3f6bca63ba63a45fa4160b6f24fcfd5f81e5af/docs/quote-page-summary.png)

*The dual RP2350 board, 5 PCBs with 2 assembled, quoted on the page from its fabrication zip.*

## Changes

- **`quote.summary`** in the library: rows for PCB fabrication, additional fees (when any), assembly (Economic PCBA when the board allows it, otherwise Standard with the reason), parts, shipping, import duties and taxes, the disbursement fee and sales tax, each with `total` and `perBoard`, then a `grandTotal` row. Fabrication is per PCB; everything else, and the grand total, is per assembled board (per PCB without assembly), so bare extra PCBs are counted in the per-board price.
- **Assembled boards may not exceed the PCB quantity.** Fewer is fine (the rest stay bare). The library throws for more, and the default of 2 assembled is capped at the PCB quantity.
- **Text output** starts with the same table, then the details.
- **Quote page**:
  - the summary table first, then additional fees and warnings, with the fabrication, assembly, shipping and BOM details folded below;
  - the form is grouped into Order, Board and Shipping;
  - the assembled-boards limit follows the PCB quantity and a mistake is explained next to the form instead of failing the quote;
  - the assembled field is disabled with "No assembly";
  - a progress bar shows part lookups;
  - it fits a phone screen without sideways scrolling.

## Testing

- `bun test` (34 tests), `bun run typecheck` and `bun run format:check` pass.
- New tests: the summary rows add up to the grand total, the quantity rules in the library and on the page.
- The built page was driven in headless Chromium with the dual RP2350 fabrication zip:
  - the table matched the text output (grand total $413.51, $206.76 per assembled board);
  - 6 assembled from 5 PCBs showed the inline error;
  - 10 PCBs with 3 assembled re-quoted from the cache;
  - no page errors, and no sideways scroll at 390 px wide.

